description:
Add a pure (no I/O, no state) helper function mapping each `SpacePatchOp` variant to its required permission strings per draft-atwood-jmap-chat-00 §Space/set lines 1093-1129. Used by backend implementations of `apply_space_patch` to gate per-op authorization (see JMAP-g7wu.2.4.3 for the canonical consumer).

Site: crate-jmap-chat-server/src/space.rs (a new module-level pub helper) or a new file crate-jmap-chat-server/src/permissions.rs.

Placement rationale: this lives in chat-server NOT chat-types. The wire types in chat-types should not know about server-side permission vocabulary. Permission strings are domain-specific to backend authorization logic.

Signature:

    /// Returns the set of permission strings required to apply this
    /// SpacePatchOp variant, per draft-atwood-jmap-chat-00 §Space/set
    /// lines 1093, 1096, 1102, 1105, 1108, 1111, 1114, 1117, 1120,
    /// 1123, 1126, 1129.
    ///
    /// Permissions enumerated by the draft:
    ///   - manage_space   — top-level metadata (name, description, iconBlobId, isPublic, isPubliclyPreviewable)
    ///   - manage_roles   — addRoles, removeRoles, updateRoles
    ///   - manage_members — addMembers, removeMembers, updateMembers (roleIds changes also require manage_roles)
    ///   - manage_channels — addChannels, removeChannels, updateChannels, addCategories, removeCategories, updateCategories
    ///
    /// This helper is pure and has no side effects. Backends consume
    /// it inside `apply_space_patch` after resolving the caller's
    /// effective permissions. Handlers MUST NOT consume this helper
    /// for permission gating — gates are backend-canonical per
    /// workspace AGENTS.md.
    pub fn required_permissions_for_op(op: &SpacePatchOp) -> &'static [&'static str];

Spec→variant→permission table (encoded in the match):

  | Variant family       | Permission(s)                          |
  |----------------------|----------------------------------------|
  | Top-level metadata   | manage_space                           |
  | AddRoles, RemoveRoles, UpdateRoles | manage_roles               |
  | AddMembers           | manage_members                         |
  | RemoveMembers        | manage_members                         |
  | UpdateMembers (with role_ids change) | manage_members + manage_roles |
  | UpdateMembers (nick only)            | manage_members                |
  | AddChannels, RemoveChannels, UpdateChannels | manage_channels       |
  | AddCategories, RemoveCategories, UpdateCategories | manage_channels |

## Acceptance

  - Helper signature exists as documented above with full doc comment.
  - Returns `&'static [&'static str]` (static slice; no allocation).
  - Unit tests cover every variant: each SpacePatchOp construction → expected permission slice. Tests use exhaustive match against the SpacePatchOp variants so that adding a new variant to the type forces this helper to be updated.
  - `cargo test -p jmap-chat-server` clean.
  - `cargo clippy -p jmap-chat-server -- -D warnings` clean.

## Out of scope

  - Caller-permission resolution (lookup of caller's effective permissions in a Space) — that lives in the backend per JMAP-g7wu.2.4.3.
  - Gating logic (deciding whether to apply or reject) — that lives in the backend.
  - Handler-side use of this helper — forbidden by workspace 'backend canonical' policy.

## Depends on

  JMAP-g7wu.2.4.1 (`SpacePatchOp` enum, closed).

## Blocks

  JMAP-g7wu.2.4.3 consumes this helper inside `apply_space_patch`. Add a blocks-link after both beads exist.
